@startuml
title VEL | Configuration-Driven Source Addition
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #4F5D75
skinparam activityBorderColor #2D3142
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activityFontColor #2D3142
skinparam diamondBorderColor #4F5D75
skinparam diamondBackgroundColor #ECECEC
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #BFC0C0

start
:Define Input Interface Definition
(RawEvidenceSchema) for the module's state
-- including, for any interface-specific
state/error field, a `conversion` block
(values map + onUnmapped: preserveOriginal);
:Define Normalization Mapping
(EvidenceNormalizationRule) for the module's state;
:Add a VehicleEvidenceCollector config
declaring source_ref/collector_id and a
fieldBindingProvider block;
if (Can the module's state be read via existing\ngeneric transport/provider capabilities,\ndeclared purely in fieldBindingProvider config?) then (yes)
  :Set fieldBindingProvider.kind: generic;
  #C8E6C9:No new code. GenericFieldBindings\n(built into VEL core) is config-driven;
else (no -- genuinely native interface)
  #FFF1E9:Implement a plugin binding\n(implements shared IStateFieldBindingProvider)\nas an INDEPENDENTLY BUILT AND DEPLOYED\nartifact, built/versioned\nseparately from VEL core;
  :Set fieldBindingProvider.kind: plugin\nwith library/entryPoint/settings;
  #C8E6C9:PluginLoader loads it at runtime via a\nstable C-ABI entry point, purely from\nthis config -- no VEL core change, no\ncollector subclass, no hard-coded\nfactory entry, no VEL core rebuild;
endif
stop

note right
No new Mapper, Validator, or Normalizer class is ever written, and no
new SCoreCollector subclass is ever written either.
ConfigDrivenStateMapper, SchemaValidator, NormalizationProcessor, and
SCoreCollector itself are shared, config-driven infrastructure (see
Collector_common_class_diagram.puml). Enum-to-string conversion for
interface-specific state/error values is likewise config-driven,
executed generically by ConfigDrivenStateMapper from each field's
`conversion` block -- never hard-coded in a binding or plugin.
No changes to common VEL processing behavior are required
(FR-VEL-012, FR-VEL-013/014/015).
end note
@enduml
